                    "message": "Will keep this on hold till the root cause is not identified."
                },
                {
                    "file": "wait-vpd-parser/src/collection_orchestrator.cpp",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "as async_method_call_timed is used, we can call io_context run here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "wait-vpd-parser/src/collection_orchestrator.cpp",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "No. Consider the scenario where `CollectAllFruVpd` returned success in about ~30 seconds, after which we start a listener on `CollectionStatus` property. \n\nIf we use `m_ioContext.run()` here, `wait-vpd-parser` will block here until Collection Status = Completed, which may take more than 6 minutes. So `wait-vpd-parsers` fails to check if collection is completed before 6 minutes.\nConsider another scenario where `vpd-manager` fails to update CollectionStatus = Complete for some reason. Then, `wait-vpd-parser` gets blocked here infinitely."
                }
            ],
